+Creating Views
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+The entry point for creating views is ``pypika.Query.create_view``. The view is defined by a query passed to
+``as_select``. Optional modifiers are ``columns``, ``or_replace``, ``temporary`` and ``if_not_exists``;
+``PostgreSQLQuery.create_view`` also offers ``materialized``.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    q = Query.from_("orders").select("id", "total").where(Field("status") == "paid")
+    Query.create_view("v_paid").or_replace().as_select(q)
+
+.. code-block:: sql
+
+    CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW "v_paid" AS SELECT "id","total" FROM "orders" WHERE "status"='paid'
+
 Creating Tables
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 
